/* book Worked example: Q: An 8-bit uniform quantizer has a range of ±1 V and a full-scale sinusoidal input. Find L, Δ, Pq and the SQNR in dB, and check the 6.02n + 1.76 rule.
   1. L = 2⁸ = 256 levels.
   2. Δ = 2V/L = 2 V/256 = 0.0078125 V = 7.8125 mV.
   3. Pq = Δ²/12 = (7.8125 × 10⁻³)²/12 = 6.1035 × 10⁻⁵/12 = 5.086 × 10⁻⁶ V².
   4. Px = V²/2 = 0.5 V², so SQNR = 0.5/5.086 × 10⁻⁶ = 98 304 = 1.5 × 256².
   5. 10 log10(98 304) = 49.93 dB; the rule gives 6.02 × 8 + 1.76 = 49.92 dB.
   Answer: L = 256, Δ = 7.8125 mV, Pq = 5.086 × 10⁻⁶ V², SQNR = 49.9 dB. */
