/* book Worked example 2: Q: Encode x(t) = 3.5 sin(2π·1000t) V with the 3-bit quantizer of the figure (±4 V, Δ = 1 V, natural binary), sampling at 8 kHz at the instants t = (k + ½)Ts, k = 0 to 7. Give the bit stream, the largest error and the bit rate.
   1. The phase at the samples is 2π·1000·(k + ½)/8000 = π/8 + kπ/4, so x = 3.5 sin(22.5°) = 1.339 V, 3.5 sin(67.5°) = 3.234 V, and so on.
   2. Round to the nearest of the eight levels and read off the code: level −3.5 V is 000, −1.5 V is 010, +1.5 V is 101, +3.5 V is 111.
   3. All errors are within ±Δ/2 = ±0.5 V; the largest is 0.266 V.
   4. Rb = 3 × 8000 = 24 kbit/s; one period (1 ms) carries 24 bits.
   Answer:  */
